                    <!-- Frequently Asked Questions -->
                    <section id="faqs">
                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                        <div class="accordion faq-accordion mt-4" id="cancellationFaqAccordion">

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading1">
                                    <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faqCollapse1">
                                        1. Can an FIR automatically result in OCI cancellation?
                                    </button>
                                </h3>
                                <div id="faqCollapse1" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" aria-labelledby="faqHeading1" data-bs-parent="#cancellationFaqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        An FIR and a charge-sheet are different procedural events. The 2025 notification addresses specified circumstances involving qualifying sentences and charge-sheets for offences punishable with imprisonment of seven years or more. The precise legal basis and facts must be examined; an FIR alone should not automatically be treated as satisfying every cancellation ground.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading2">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse2">
                                        2. Can OCI registration be cancelled before a criminal conviction?
                                    </button>
                                </h3>
                                <div id="faqCollapse2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading2" data-bs-parent="#cancellationFaqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        The answer depends on the statutory ground invoked. The 2025 notification expressly addresses certain charge-sheet circumstances as well as specified sentences. The offence, applicable punishment, chronology and legal requirements must be checked.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading3">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse3">
                                        3. Does every OCI cancellation notice lead to cancellation?
                                    </button>
                                </h3>
                                <div id="faqCollapse3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading3" data-bs-parent="#cancellationFaqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        No such conclusion should be assumed. A notice initiates or communicates a process whose legal effect depends on its terms and the subsequent decision. The cardholder should respond through the applicable procedure and provide relevant evidence.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading4">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse4">
                                        4. Must the Government provide an opportunity of hearing?
                                    </button>
                                </h3>
                                <div id="faqCollapse4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading4" data-bs-parent="#cancellationFaqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        Section 7D contains a proviso requiring a reasonable opportunity of being heard before an order under that section is passed. The specific procedure and adequacy of the opportunity must be assessed in the circumstances.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading5">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse5">
                                        5. Can an OCI cardholder challenge blacklisting or refusal of entry?
                                    </button>
                                </h3>
                                <div id="faqCollapse5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading5" data-bs-parent="#cancellationFaqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        Depending on the facts and applicable law, a legal challenge may be available. The relevant immigration order, statutory basis and procedural safeguards should be examined separately from the OCI registration itself.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading6">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse6">
                                        6. Does the 2025 notification apply to every criminal case that began earlier?
                                    </button>
                                </h3>
                                <div id="faqCollapse6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading6" data-bs-parent="#cancellationFaqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        Its application to a particular matter requires legal analysis. The dates of the underlying events, charge-sheet, notice and proposed or final order may be important. Litigation has raised questions about the notification's scope and temporal application; no universal conclusion should be drawn without checking the current legal position.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading7">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse7">
                                        7. Can an OCI cancellation order be challenged under Article 226?
                                    </button>
                                </h3>
                                <div id="faqCollapse7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading7" data-bs-parent="#cancellationFaqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        A High Court challenge may be available in an appropriate case. Maintainability, grounds, relief and the applicable procedure depend on the actual order and facts. A writ petition does not guarantee a favourable result.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="accordion-item">
                                <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading8">
                                    <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse8">
                                        8. Should I continue travelling to India after receiving a cancellation notice?
                                    </button>
                                </h3>
                                <div id="faqCollapse8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading8" data-bs-parent="#cancellationFaqAccordion">
                                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                        Do not assume that a notice has the same effect as a final cancellation order, or that an existing OCI card necessarily resolves every immigration concern. Before travelling, verify the current status and any separate immigration directions applicable to you.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                        </div>
